spec:
  grid: 7-19 rows x 7-19 cols, always square [observed]
  background: single color (orange/7 in all examples [observed])
  rectangle:
    shape: solid filled rectangle, single non-bg color (grey/5 [observed])
    size: 3-17 wide x 4-9 tall
    position: bottom row always touches grid bottom; >=1 row of bg above for markers
    side_clearance: >=1 col of bg on exit side (so teal can land outside the rect)
  markers:
    count: exactly 1 red (2) and 1 teal (8), each a single cell
    row: both on the same row, exactly 1 row above the rectangle top
    columns: both within the rectangle's column range, different columns
    separation: 2-5 cols apart
  transformation:
    - clear original red to bg
    - recolor teal's cell to red
    - place teal at (rect_bottom_row, exit_col) where exit_col is c0-1 if teal is left of red, c1+1 if teal is right of red

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick square grid size N in [7..19]. Choose bg and rect_color (distinct, neither red nor teal).
    2. Pick rect dimensions (w in [3..N-2], h in [3..N-3]) ensuring at least 1 empty row above for marker row and at least 1 col on one side for exit.
    3. Place rect so its bottom row = N-1. Choose horizontal position ensuring >=1 col clearance on at least one side.
    4. Pick exit_side (left or right) where clearance >=1. Compute exit_col = c0-1 or c1+1. Place teal at (rect_bottom_row, exit_col).
    5. Pick teal_marker_col inside rect col range. Set red_marker_col also inside rect col range, on the opposite side of teal_marker_col relative to exit direction (if exit right, red is left of teal; if exit left, red is right of teal). Ensure separation >=2.
    6. Place red at (rect_top-1, red_marker_col) and teal-becomes-red at (rect_top-1, teal_marker_col).
    7. To get the INPUT from this output: move red from teal_marker_col back to red_marker_col, change that cell to red; clear the exit teal cell to bg; place teal at (rect_top-1, teal_marker_col) and red at (rect_top-1, red_marker_col).
