0015: def main(input_grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0016:     """
0017:     Crop the colored rectangle frame and connect scattered pixels to the same-colored frame side.
0018: 
0019:     Input structure:
0020:     - Four full non-black lines form a rectangle on a black background.
0021:     - Each frame side has a distinct color.
0022:     - Extra scattered pixels share the color of exactly one frame side.
0023: 
0024:     Rule:
0025:     - Locate the two full horizontal and two full vertical frame lines.
0026:     - Identify the scattered pixel color outside those lines.
0027:     - Crop to the frame and draw straight connections from each scattered pixel to the matching-colored side.
0028: 
0029:     Key insight:
0030:     - The scattered pixel color selects which frame side to connect to after the rectangle
0031:       is cropped out of the larger grid.
